    {
      "incorrect": "After an hour, I could open the door.",
      "correct": "After an hour, I managed to open the door.",
      "note": "For one success in the past, use **managed to** or **was able to**; **could** is for a general ability. In the negative, all three are possible: *I couldn't open the door*."
